{#
   Scouting & Transfers (#scouting) — new in the redesign.

   Two decorative sprite scenes plus three copy cards. The scenes are generated
   client-side from seeded random configs (see landing.js's scene composer, ported
   from design/random.js.src) rather than drawn from any club's real data — these
   are illustrations of a scout and a row of agents, not a claim about anybody's
   squad. Everything on the page that renders REAL data (the Club Spotlight, the
   Rich List, the telemetry badges) is kept visually distinct by living inside a
   ringed panel; these sit bare on the section background.

   data-scene names the composition landing.js builds; the alt text is authored
   here because it describes the content, and the sizes reserve the aspect box so
   a late-mounting sprite causes no layout shift.
#}
<section class="scouting-section" id="scouting" aria-labelledby="scouting-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-label">Scouting &amp; Transfers</div>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="scouting-title">NEVER BUY BLIND</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">Every signing runs the same chain. Your Lead Scout files a report, the Director of Football sets it against recruitment priorities, the Manager weighs in on squad fit, and the final offer still needs your sign-off.</p>

        <div class="scouting-grid">
            <figure class="scene-figure">
                <div class="scene" data-scene="scout1">
                    <img alt="Pixel scout standing beside two young prospects" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <figcaption class="vt">Your DoF sets the priorities. You set the budget.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="scene-figure">
                <div class="scene" data-scene="scout2">
                    <img alt="Three pixel agents in suits" width="520" height="400" decoding="async">
                </div>
                <figcaption class="vt">Six agent tiers, from Elite down to Unknown.</figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="scouting-points">
                <article class="pillar-card">
                    <h3 class="pillar-title">SCARCITY BY DESIGN</h3>
                    <p>Every player in the pool is a single, real entity. Sign one and they are gone for everyone else. No restocks, no duplicates.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="pillar-card">
                    <h3 class="pillar-title">BUY THE DOSSIER</h3>
                    <p>The best agents' books are locked until you pay. Unlock a full client list and you unlock preferred rates on every player they represent.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="pillar-card">
                    <h3 class="pillar-title">NO BANKRUPTCY</h3>
                    <p>Navigate agent personalities, sign-on fees and squad-role expectations without going bankrupt.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
